// {1}{G} sorcery: "Target creature you control fights target creature you
// don't control." (Prey Upon's shape, [CR#701.14a].) The fight family's TWO
// same-sort targets are the R2 ambiguity gate's canonical expected firer
// ([[cards-corpus-dry-run]]): an anaphoric read (`It`/`That(Creature)`) of
// either target would be a guess. The sunset's announce-list labeling story
// ([[cards-fidelity-target-sunset]]) names each slot with `As` and reads it
// back with `The` ([CR#608.2d] labeled antecedents) — the labeled slots still
// participate in R1/R2 exactly like unlabeled ones (this fixture pins that
// the gate stayed frozen), and the explicit reads are never a guess.
Normal(
    name: "Sorcery Fight Two Targets",
    mana_cost: [Generic(1), Green],
    types: [Sorcery],
    abilities: [
        Spell(effect: Targeted(
            targets: [
                As("first", TargetOne(AllOf([Creature, ControlledBy(Ref(You))]))),
                As("second", TargetOne(AllOf([Creature, Not(ControlledBy(Ref(You)))]))),
            ],
            effect: Fight(The("first"), The("second")),
        )),
    ],
)
